## Why This Is Asked

This tests a standard DP with an adjacency constraint and a limit on picks, plus reconstruction.

## Key Concepts

- DP over i and t with i-2 due to adjacency
- Reconstruction via a take/parent trace
- Space/time trade-offs; potential optimizations

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxNonAdjSum(a, k) {
  const n = a.length;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(0));
  const take = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(false));
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
      dp[i][t] = dp[i-1][t];
      if (t > 0 && i >= 2 && dp[i-2][t-1] + a[i-1] > dp[i][t]) {
        dp[i][t] = dp[i-2][t-1] + a[i-1];
        take[i][t] = true;
      }
    }
  }
  // Reconstruct indices
  const indices = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (i > 0 && t > 0) {
    if (take[i][t]) {
      indices.push(i-1);
      i -= 2;
      t--;
    } else {
      i--;
    }
  }
  return { maxProfit: dp[n][k], indices: indices.reverse() };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP design when block value is nonlinear in length and sum, forcing nontrivial transitions and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Non-overlapping subarrays DP, prefix sums, reconstruction pointers
- Time/space trade-offs with O(n^2 k) baseline, potential optimizations
- Handling exact k blocks and base cases

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKBlocks(A, k){
  const n=A.length; const S=[0]; for(const x of A) S.push(S[S.length-1]+x);
  const dp=Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1e15));
  const prv=Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(null));
  dp[0][0]=0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=0;t<=k;t++){
      dp[i][t]=dp[i-1][t];
      if(t>0){
        for(let l=1;l<=i;l++){
          const sum=S[i]-S[l-1];
          const val=dp[l-1][t-1]+sum*(i-l+1);
          if(val>dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t]=val; prv[i][t]=l; }
        }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction omitted for brevity
  return {best:dp[n][k]};
}
```

