## Why This Is Asked
This problem combines two key challenges: optimizing over two sequences simultaneously and selecting exactly k non-overlapping intervals. It tests your ability to formulate dynamic programming solutions for constrained partitioning problems and handle solution reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- 2D prefix sums for O(1) range sum queries
- Non-overlapping interval DP with exact count constraint
- Path reconstruction via backpointers
- Trade-off between intervals via knapsack-like combining

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxIntervalValue(A, B, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const PA = [0], PB = [0];
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    PA[i] = PA[i-1] + A[i-1];
    PB[i] = PB[i-1] + B[i-1];
  }
  const dp = Array(n+1).fill(null).map(() => Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const prev = Array(n+1).fill(null).map(() => Array(k+1).fill(null));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let r = 1; r <= n; r++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      for (let l = 1; l <= r; l++) {
        const val = (PA[r] - PA[l-1]) * (PB[r] - PB[l-1]);
        const candidate = dp[l-1][t-1] + val;
        if (candidate > dp[r][t]) {
          dp[r][t] = candidate;
          prev[r][t] = { l, r: l-1 };
        }
      }
    }
  }
  return dp[n][k];
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to craft DP with a left-anchored subarray value and exact block counts, plus reconstruction for endpoints.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP with exactly k blocks
- Precomputation of bestStartAt[l][i]
- Reconstructing block boundaries via parent pointers
- Time/space trade-offs and potential optimizations

## Code Example
```javascript
function computeBestStartDP(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let i=0;i<n;i++) pref[i+1] = pref[i] + A[i];
  const bestStart = Array.from({length:n}, ()=> Array(n).fill(-Infinity));
  for (let l=0; l<n; l++) {
    let best = -Infinity;
    for (let i=l; i<n; i++) {
      const sum = pref[i+1]-pref[l];
      best = Math.max(best, sum);
      bestStart[l][i] = best;
    }
  }
  const dp = Array.from({length:n}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({length:n}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for (let i=0; i<n; i++) dp[i][1] = bestStart[0][i];
  for (let t=2; t<=k; t++) {
    for (let i=t-1; i<n; i++) {
      let bestVal = -Infinity, bestL = -1;
      for (let l=t-1; l<=i; l++) {
        const prev = (l-1>=0) ? dp[l-1][t-1] : (t-1===0 ? 0 : -Infinity);
        const val = prev + bestStart[l][i];
        if (val > bestVal) { bestVal = val; bestL = l; }
      }
      dp[i][t] = bestVal;
      par[i][t] = bestL;
    }
  }
  return {dp, par};
}
```

